2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
“approved urine specimen handling machine” means a machine approved by the Director to carry out the function of handling urine specimens;
[S 429/2026 wef 01/07/2026]
“approved urine specimen labelling machine” means a machine approved by the Director to carry out the function of labelling bottles and test tubes used to process urine specimens;
[S 429/2026 wef 01/07/2026]
“approved urine specimen sealing machine” means a machine approved by the Director to carry out the function of sealing urine specimens;
[S 429/2026 wef 01/07/2026]
“Chief Executive of the Health Sciences Authority” means the Chief Executive of the Health Sciences Authority appointed under section 15 of the Health Sciences Authority Act 2001;
[Deleted by S 429/2026 wef 01/07/2026]
“DSO National Laboratories” means the company incorporated under the Companies Act 1967 as DSO National Laboratories (UEN 199701777M);
[S 797/2025 wef 15/12/2025]
“enforcement officer” means an officer of the Central Narcotics Bureau, an immigration officer, a police officer not below the rank of sergeant, a serviceman in the Singapore Armed Forces who is appointed by the Minister as an enforcement officer under section 31(1B) of the Act or a supervision officer appointed under regulation 15(1) of the Misuse of Drugs (Approved Institutions, Medical Observation and Treatment and Rehabilitation) Regulations (Rg 3).
[S 141/2001 wef 01/04/2001]
[S 713/2020 wef 31/08/2020]
[S 429/2026 wef 01/07/2026]
